  },
  {
   "id": "e01581",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 5440,
   "width": 610.5,
   "height": 37.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": "e01456",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1442898017,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1634261033,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1760000000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Hypergeometric, no replacement. With about 100 lane A clusters you still check 39 to rule out 5%. Sampling pays\noff only on large lanes, so: review every lane A cluster (1.5 min each, keyboard) and use sampling for PE, UX\nand NU audits instead.",
   "fontSize": 10,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "Hypergeometric, no replacement. With about 100 lane A clusters you still check 39 to rule out 5%. Sampling pays\noff only on large lanes, so: review every lane A cluster (1.5 min each, keyboard) and use sampling for PE, UX\nand NU audits instead.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "e01582",
